#### 1.4.5 Based on the three different bootstrap sample lengths in 3. compute the corresponding 0.025 and 0.975 quantiles. Compare the three resulting intervals against each other.

In this task, we will compute the 95% confidence intervals for the median using three different bootstrap sample sizes: 20, 200, and 2000. For each set of bootstrap medians, we will calculate the 0.025 and 0.975 quantiles to define the confidence intervals. By comparing these intervals, we can assess how the precision of the confidence interval improves as the number of bootstrap samples increases and how the different sample sizes influence the stability and reliability of the resulting intervals.

